      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am still suggesting move this statement of wait WIP from before clearing interrupt to the after, the reasons are below:\n1: WIP means writing to corresponding register is not finish, so if no write before or pevious write already finish then this bit is cleared.\n2: this will make sure interrupt is actually cleared before further processing.\n3: since this is the only place to clear interrupt status (correct me if I am wrong) put wait WIP after clearing interrupt also guarantees next write is valid without need to wait for WIP and covers the effect of put wait WIP before clearing interrupt.",
